From: Darrel Griët <dgriet@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] backports: Drop the trailing slash from BACKPORT_DIR

Every Kconfig file of the integrated backports tree is pulled in as
source "$BACKPORT_DIR/.../Kconfig". With BACKPORT_DIR set to "backports/"
those expand to paths carrying a double slash, e.g.

    backports//drivers/net/wireless/Kconfig

kconfig itself copes, but it records the names verbatim in
include/config/auto.conf.cmd, both in $(deps_config) and in the catch-all
"$(deps_config): ;" rule. In an out-of-tree build ($B != $S, as used by
linux-yocto.inc) those prerequisites are relative to the build directory and
have to be resolved through VPATH = $(srctree). GNU make's VPATH search does
not handle "//" inside a file name, so all 157 of them are treated as
non-existent, the empty recipe "makes" them, and include/config/auto.conf is
left permanently out of date.

Since auto.conf is an included makefile, make regenerates it via
silentoldconfig and then restarts - forever. The build never reaches a single
CC, it just loops on:

      GEN     .../linux-tetra-standard-build/Makefile
    scripts/kconfig/conf --silentoldconfig Kconfig

Dropping the trailing slash makes every source path single-slashed and lets
VPATH resolve them. CONFIG_BACKPORT_DIR has no other consumer: backports/Makefile
defines its own make-level BACKPORT_DIR.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [android vendor kernel]
---
 backports/Kconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/backports/Kconfig b/backports/Kconfig
index 5bc32035cf7..fd740b58433 100644
--- a/backports/Kconfig
+++ b/backports/Kconfig
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@ config BACKPORT_INTEGRATE

 config BACKPORT_DIR
 	string
-	default "backports/"
+	default "backports"

 config BACKPORT_VERSION
 	string
